## STEP 4 — SELF-CRITIQUE

- [PARKED] CORS wildcard (aggregated [65]): re-confirmed dead — no `access-control-allow-credentials`, cross-origin JS cannot carry x-gladia-key; no exploitable cross-origin read
- [PARKED] legacy /audio|/video endpoints as standalone hypothesis: merged into H1 — same class/gateway, no evidence yet that path is independently weaker
- [PARKED] /health runtime leak: probed `?full=true` — bare `{"health":"OK"}`, no verbose output; remains low-severity accepted MISCONFIG, no escalation
- [PARKED] OpenAPI shadow-endpoint enumeration: stays parked (active fuzzing prohibited under passive-first)
- [FINAL] ranked: 1) H1 SSRF @ api.gladia.io (70, SDK+spec-confirmed fetch surface) | 2) H3 npm impersonation (78, verified fact, PASSIVE) | 3) H2 open redirect @ app.gladia.io (55, needs session)

## STEP 5 — NEXT ACTION

[NEXT] HUMAN: with a program-provided or personal trial `x-gladia-key`, POST https://api.gladia.io/v2/pre-recorded `{"audio_url":"http://<attacker-canary>"}` then `{"audio_url":"http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/"}`; compare job error_code/status/timing for reachability signal; then repeat via https://api.gladia.io/video/text/video-transcription `video_url` to test the legacy fetch path.

